
Analysis Description
--------------------
Examine whether or not a codon alignment is better fit by models which
permit multiple instantaneous substitutions. v0.2 adds a separate rate
for codon-island triple-hit rates

- __Requirements__: in-frame codon alignment and a phylogenetic tree

- __Citation__: Submitted; preprint at hyphy.org/resources/fmm.pdf

- __Written by__: Sergei L Kosakovsky Pond, Sadie Wisotsky and Alexander Lucaci

- __Contact Information__: spond@temple.edu

- __Analysis Version__: 1.0


>code => Universal
>Loaded a multiple sequence alignment with **18** sequences, **342** codons, and **1** partitions from `/Users/alex/Documents/selection-tutorial/data/21-empirical/flavNS5.nex`
The number of omega rate classes to include in the model (permissible range = [1,10], default value = 3, integer): 
>rates => 3

>triple-islands => No


### Obtaining branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases under the nucleotide GTR model

>kill-zero-lengths => Yes
* Log(L) = -11349.07, AIC-c = 22780.32 (41 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site)  2.714

### Obtaining the global omega estimate based on relative GTR branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases
* Log(L) = -9584.49, AIC-c = 19265.75 (48 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site)  4.431
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio for *test* =   0.0593

### Fitting Standard MG94
* Log(L) = -9140.02, AIC-c = 18386.98 (53 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.0470
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.055               |    63.903     |                                   |
|               1.489               |    26.505     |                                   |
|               5.947               |     9.592     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -9088.13, AIC-c = 18285.24 (54 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.0341
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.7208
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.090               |    67.162     |                                   |
|               1.809               |    25.416     |                                   |
|               6.465               |     7.422     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double and triple instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -9085.91, AIC-c = 18282.83 (55 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.0345
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.5093
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.6837
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon between synonymous codon islands =   0.6837
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.088               |    66.719     |                                   |
|               1.793               |    25.740     |                                   |
|               6.358               |     7.541     |                                   |


